flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the<br/>encoder scale for scratches, oil, or coolant<br/>deposits. 2. Check the read head mounting for<br/>looseness or impact damage. 3. Inspect the cable and<br/>connector for chafing or corrosion."]
    box_2{"Physical damage to encoder strip or read head?"}
    box_3(["End, Escalate: physical damage, replace encoder<br/>assembly"])
    box_4["Connect a digital oscilloscope to the encoder A and<br/>B channel outputs at the drive amplifier input<br/>terminals. Command slow axis movement and verify<br/>that both channels produce clean square waves with<br/>90 degree phase separation and no missing pulses.<br/>Record the peak to peak voltage and compare against<br/>the encoder data sheet specification."]
    box_5[/"Refer to the encoder signal specification."/]
    box_6{"Signal quality: clean waveform, no dropouts?"}
    box_7["Clean encoder strip with lint free cloth and<br/>isopropyl alcohol"]
    box_8{"Reverify signal quality after strip cleaning"}
    box_9(["End, Replace encoder strip: signal quality<br/>unrecoverable"])
    box_10["Command a homing cycle from the machine controller<br/>and observe the axis motion from the controller<br/>position display. The axis should decelerate<br/>smoothly on the home switch trigger and come to rest<br/>at the reference mark position. Confirm the<br/>displayed home offset matches the value stored in<br/>the machine parameter table."]
    box_11{"Reference mark found during homing cycle?"}
    box_12["Reteach home offset, adjust reference mark position"]
    box_13["Command the axis to move to each of ten programmed<br/>reference positions distributed across the full<br/>travel, pausing two seconds at each point. At each<br/>position, record the encoder feedback value and the<br/>commanded position from the controller display.<br/>Calculate the maximum positioning error across the<br/>grid and compare against the axis accuracy<br/>specification."]
    box_14[/"Refer to the position accuracy specification."/]
    box_15{"Position accuracy within tolerance at all test<br/>points?"}
    box_16["Adjust read head gap to encoder strip per<br/>specification"]
    box_17{"Reverify position accuracy after read head<br/>adjustment"}
    box_18(["End, Escalate: encoder calibration by metrology<br/>required"])
    box_19[/"Refer to the thermal compensation table."/]
    box_20{"Thermal compensation parameter active and correct?"}
    box_21["Complete the following checks: 1. Read the thermal<br/>compensation coefficient from the controller<br/>parameter screen. 2. Compare the stored coefficient<br/>against the reference value for this machine. 3.<br/>Check whether the compensation model was modified<br/>since the last calibration."]
    box_22["Trace the encoder cable from the read head to the<br/>drive amplifier, checking for sharp bends at conduit<br/>entries, contact with rotating parts, or unsupported<br/>lengths that can flex during high speed movement.<br/>Confirm that strain relief clamps are tight and<br/>positioned within 100 millimetres of each connector.<br/>Gently flex the cable at any suspected damage point<br/>while monitoring the encoder signal for glitches."]
    box_23{"Cable condition and routing acceptable?"}
    box_24["Reroute cable and fit strain relief clamps"]
    box_25{"Final 5 point position verification cycle passed?"}
    box_26["Log encoder service data and update maintenance<br/>record"]
    box_27(["End, Procedure complete"])

